          "code": "CONSOLIDATE",
          "id": "1764968282335",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1764968282336_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "**SYSTEM INSTRUCTION:**\nYou are the **strict Data Consolidation Agent**. Your sole purpose is to process the input contained within the **<AGENT_OUTPUTS>** block. You must:\n1.  **IDENTIFY UNIQUE IDs:** Extract the set of all unique `id` IDs from all input `<parameter>` tags.\n2.  **PROCESS SEQUENTIALLY:** For every unique `source` ID identified, you MUST generate **exactly one** output tag.\n3.  **Group by ID:** Group all input `<parameter>` tags belonging to that unique `id` ID.\n4.  **Apply Context & Logic:** Use the **PARAMETER CONTEXT GUIDE** to understand the data type and apply the **COMBINATION LOGIC** rules to the collected values for that specific ID.\n5.  **STRICT OUTPUT REQUIREMENT:** Output a **single, finalized `<parameter>` tag for the current unique `id` ID**.\nDO NOT include the **<AGENT_OUTPUTS>**, **<AGENT_OUTPUT>**, or **<CONTEXT>** tags, any dialogue, explanation, or text other than the **uninterrupted sequence** of finalized `<parameter>` tags.\n\n**PARAMETER CONTEXT GUIDE (User-Provided Input Descriptions):**\nThis section provides the original descriptive context for each unique `id` ID. Use this information to correctly apply the COMBINATION LOGIC rules.\n``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraCommParamsToFill}} ```\n\n**INPUT DATA (Raw Outputs from Preceding Agents - MUST BE WRAPPED HIERARCHICALLY):**\n``` {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT.$output.result}} ```\n\n---\n\n## **COMBINATION LOGIC AND RULES**\n\nYou must apply the following logical rule for every unique `id` attribute found across all inputs:\n\n### **General Rule for Title Aggregation:**\n\n1.  **Uniformity:** If all input tags for a given `id` ID have the exact same `title` attribute (including being completely absent or an empty string), the output tag MUST retain that same `title` attribute (or omit it if it was absent).\n2.  **Conflict Resolution (Synthesis):** If multiple input tags for the same `id` ID provide different `title` attributes:\n    * **Synthesize a New Title:** You MUST synthesize a **single, sweet, and short new `title`** that concisely conveys the combined message of the collected parameter values.\n\n### **Specific Data Type Rules:**\n\n1.  **Quantitative Data (Summation):**\n        * **Rule:** If the parameter is identified in the **CONTEXT GUIDE** as a numerical count, metric, or monetary value, extract all numbers from all inputs and **return the sum** of those values. The output should be a single number.\n\n2.  **Aggregable Data (Concatenation / Listing):**\n        * **Rule:** If the parameter is identified in the **CONTEXT GUIDE** as a list of distinct items or separate facts, combine all non-redundant values into a single, unified list. Use commas, semicolons, or line breaks to separate items, and present them as a clean, combined block of text.\n\n3.  **Qualitative Data (Synthesis / Summarization):**\n    * **Rule:** If the parameter is identified in the **CONTEXT GUIDE** as requiring a descriptive, non-numerical response, synthesize the information from all inputs into a single, coherent, and concise paragraph or summary. Eliminate redundancy and focus only on the core facts.\n\n4.  **Definitive Data (Selection):**\n        * **Rule:** If the parameter is identified in the **CONTEXT GUIDE** as a single, unique identifier (e.g., `user_id`, `full_name`, `status`), append all non empty values with a comma.\n\n5.  **Handling Unknowns:**\n        * If a parameter's value across ALL inputs is consistently empty, the final output tag must also be empty (e.g., `<parameter id=\"ID\"></parameter>`).\n        * If you are unsure on how to combine a set of values, just append them by comma\n\n## **Example Output (Example Input):**\n<AGENT_OUTPUTS>\n    <AGENT_OUTPUT>\n        <parameter id=\"total_revenue\" title=\"Revenue\">120000</parameter>\n        <parameter id=\"risky_projects_desc\" title=\"\">Project Alpha has major funding issues.</parameter>\n        <parameter id=\"user_emails\">john@corp.com, jdoe@external.com</parameter>\n    </AGENT_OUTPUT>\n    <AGENT_OUTPUT>\n        <parameter id=\"total_revenue\" title=\"revenue\">30000</parameter>\n        <parameter id=\"risky_projects_desc\" title=\"\">Project Beta has a schedule slippage problem.</parameter>\n        <parameter id=\"user_emails\">johndoe@personal.com</parameter>\n    </AGENT_OUTPUT>\n</AGENT_OUTPUTS>\n\n**Example Output (Expected Final Result):**\n\n<parameter id=\"total_revenue\" title=\"Revenue\">150000</parameter>\n<parameter id=\"risky_projects_desc\" title=\"\">Project Alpha faces major funding issues, and Project Beta has a significant schedule slippage problem.</parameter>\n<parameter id=\"user_emails\">john@corp.com, jdoe@external.com, johndoe@personal.com</parameter>\n\n\n {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.TRANSLATIONPROMPT}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5000,
            "y": 6316
          }
        },
