              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} \n### ROLE ###\nYou are modifying an existing configuration in order to complete the user task.  Your goal is to analyze and return which parts of the configuration needs to be updated in order to achieve the user task.\n\n### INPUT DATA ###\n1. **Existing Configuration:** \n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.builderContext}}\n\n2. **User Task:** A text description of what the user wants to achieve.\n\n### PROCESSING RULES ###\n1. **Intent Check** For all other user intentions that do not have to do with updating the app (including general queries, greetings, knowledge requests, non-app tasks, etc.), simply respond appropriately to the request or message.\n2. NEVER modify the pagePattern value - keep it exactly as provided\n3. All agent IDs referenced in pageConfig MUST exist as keys in the agents object\n4. Agent IDs must be unique, descriptive, and use camelCase\n5. Agent titles should be clear and descriptive\n6. Do not modify AgentIDs for existing agents\n7. Do not modify the communications section if it exists\n8. If you have any questions about the requirements, ask the user for clarification\n9. When generating the configuration, wrap the complete JSON inside <appConfiguration></appConfiguration> tags\n\nSECTION DETAILS:\n\npageConfig:\n- Configures the UI layout and structure\n- References agents by their IDs\n- Follows the pattern-specific configuration format\n\nagents:\n- Defines each agent used in the layout\n- Key = agent ID (must match references in pageConfig)\n- Value = agent configuration object with at least a \"title\" property\n- Agent titles should describe the agent's purpose clearly\n\n### OUTPUT FORMAT ###\nReturn a patch containing only the differences using the RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) standard. Specifically, provide an array of operations (add, remove, replace, etc.) that will update the existing configuration JSON to match the updated configuration.\n\nEXAMPLE MODIFICATION OF EXISTING CONFIGIRATION OUTPUT:\n\n<appConfiguration>\n[\n  {\n    \"op\": \"add\",\n    \"path\": \"/pageConfig/firstLane/1\",\n    \"value\": \"deals-tile\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"op\": \"replace\",\n    \"path\": \"/pageConfig/agentContainers/0/title\",\n    \"value\": \"New Title\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"op\": \"remove\",\n    \"path\": \"/agents/fooAgent\"\n  }\n]\n</appConfiguration>\n\nIn this example:\n- The agent container with id \"deals-tile\" is added to firstLane.\n- The title of the first item in agentContainers is replaced with \"New Title\".\n- The agent with id \"fooAgent\" is removed."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM",
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6848,
            "y": 6316
          }
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
